The separate stage is left out of the stage list when SEPARATE is off, rather than kept as a stage that
does nothing: a no-op stage would still print "[2/5] separate" and count as a step on every run. Switching
the setting still re-runs transcription, because transcribe's upstream result changes (extract's instead of
separate's) and SEPARATE is also in transcribe's settings, so that does not depend on the stage order.

Demucs is an extra, not a dependency, because most videos do not need it and it adds a model download and
about 1.2x the video's length on CPU. The stage imports it lazily and turns a missing demucs into an
install hint. The check accepts "demucs.api" as well as "demucs", because a module blocked in sys.modules
(as in the test) is reported under the submodule's name.

background.wav is still written although subtitles never use it: separate.py is copied unchanged from
video-translator.
